f the World Cup tournament itself and  the essential set of online and offline  exhibition matches all 203 officially  recognized FIFA national teams are  included and available for your  selection allowing you to undo the  injustice associated with the likes of  Sweden and Poland failing to qualify for  this summer's part of  what makes World Cup Brazil a genuinely  different proposition to other recent  FIFA titles is the care and dedication  that's gone into the little details that  manages that shouting command from the  sidelines cutaways to fans celebrating  goals in front of screens in their home  country unfortunately the graphical  quality of the crowds remains as  terrible as they've ever been on ps3 and  xbox360 but at least there's more  variety this time around it's best to  consider 2014 FIFA World Cup Brazil is a  less serious or accessible accompaniment  to the main feeder series focus more on  giving players a good climb than it is  on driving the quest for realism and  sports games this is a football game  that's perfect the fans that are looking  for a way to pass the hours between  World Cup matches this summer beyond  that it may not be as exhaustive as the  likes of FIFA 14 but with its own  distinct feel and modes to explore  there's more than enough here to keep  you satisfied before FIFA 15 lands later  in the year  [Music]

